## 1. Real-Time Streaming Architecture: Server-Sent Events (SSE)

### Why Server-Sent Events (SSE) over WebSockets?
| Feature | Server-Sent Events (SSE) | WebSockets |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Protocol** | Standard HTTP/HTTPS (`text/event-stream`) | Full-duplex TCP upgrade (`ws://`) |
| **Directionality** | Server-to-Client (ideal for progress reporting) | Bi-directional (unnecessary overhead) |
| **Reconnection** | Native automatic browser reconnection | Requires manual ping/pong & reconnection logic |
| **Proxy / Next.js Support**| Works seamlessly across proxies, Next.js API routes, and cloud hosts | Requires specialized socket servers or sticky sessions |
| **Payload** | UTF-8 JSON events | Binary / Text frames |

